  "content": {
    "id": "p93-q6-11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Find the Cartesian equation of the following, stating any restrictions where necessary.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p93-q6-11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\left(\\sqrt{2t-1},\\ t+2\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\dfrac{x^2+5}{2}$, where $x\\ge0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=2t-1\\\\t&=\\frac{x^2+1}{2}\\\\y&=\\frac{x^2+1}{2}+2\\\\y&=\\frac{x^2+5}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $x=\\sqrt{2t-1}$, $x\\ge0$. The endpoint $x=0$ occurs when $t=\\tfrac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p93-q6-11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\left(3,\\ \\dfrac{t^2+4}{2}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3$, where $y\\ge2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{t^2+4}{2}\\\\y&=\\frac{t^2}{2}+2\\\\y&\\ge2\\end{align*}$$\nThe $x$-coordinate is always $3$. Every $y\\ge2$ is attained, including $y=2$ when $t=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p93-q6-11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\left(\\sqrt{t}+1,\\ 2t-4\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=2x^2-4x-2$, where $x\\ge1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x-1&=\\sqrt{t}\\\\t&=(x-1)^2\\\\y&=2(x-1)^2-4\\\\y&=2x^2-4x-2\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\sqrt{t}\\ge0$, $x\\ge1$, with equality when $t=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p93-q6-11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\left(1+2\\sin t,\\ 2-\\sin t\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\dfrac52-\\dfrac{x}{2}$, where $-1\\le x\\le3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin t&=\\frac{x-1}{2}\\\\y&=2-\\frac{x-1}{2}\\\\y&=\\frac52-\\frac{x}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $-1\\le\\sin t\\le1$, the attainable restriction is $-1\\le x\\le3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p93-q6-11-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\left(1-2\\sin t,\\ 4\\cos^2t+1\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=4+2x-x^2$, where $-1\\le x\\le3$.\n\nEliminate $t$ using $\\cos^2t=1-\\sin^2t$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin t&=\\frac{1-x}{2}\\\\\\cos^2t&=1-\\sin^2t\\\\y&=4\\left[1-\\left(\\frac{1-x}{2}\\right)^2\\right]+1\\\\y&=5-(1-x)^2\\\\y&=4+2x-x^2\\end{align*}$$\nSince $-1\\le\\sin t\\le1$, $-1\\le x\\le3$; both endpoints are attained.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p93-q6-11-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\left(3+4\\cos^2t,\\ 3\\sin^2t-1\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3x+4y=17$, where $3\\le x\\le7$.\n\nSubstitute the isolated squared trigonometric terms into $\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t=1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos^2t&=\\frac{x-3}{4}\\\\\\sin^2t&=\\frac{y+1}{3}\\\\\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t&=1\\\\\\frac{x-3}{4}+\\frac{y+1}{3}&=1\\\\3(x-3)+4(y+1)&=12\\\\3x+4y&=17\\end{align*}$$\nSince $0\\le\\cos^2t\\le1$, the attainable restriction is $3\\le x\\le7$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      }
    ]
  },
